From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 16:09:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] ui/dbus: only claim a GL context for consoles that need
 one

The D-Bus display attaches its GL context to every graphic console it
finds, whether or not the device behind that console has anything to do
with GL:

    if (qemu_console_is_graphic(con) && dd->gl_mode != DISPLAY_GL_MODE_OFF)
        qemu_console_set_display_gl_ctx(con, &dd->glctx);

Only its own listeners are ever compatible with that context
(dbus_is_compatible_dcl), so once "-display dbus,gl=on" is in use, no
other display backend can attach to any console of that machine. A VM
with a virtio-vga-gl head for the D-Bus client and a plain virtio-vga
head for a VNC server fails to start:

    qemu-system-x86_64: Display vnc is incompatible with the GL context

even though VNC asked for the plain head by name with
"-vnc :1,display=video1,head=0", and that head's device never requested
GL.

Devices already state whether they need a GL context: virtio-gpu sets
GRAPHIC_FLAGS_GL only when virgl is enabled (virtio_gpu_virgl_enabled),
and console_compatible_with() consumes the same flag to decide whether a
console *requires* GL. Use it here too, so the D-Bus display takes
ownership of exactly the consoles that asked for it and leaves the rest
available to other backends.

The GL head keeps its zero-copy dmabuf scanout; the plain head becomes
usable by VNC, SPICE or any other listener at the same time.

Rebased onto QEMU 11.1.2.

Signed-off-by: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
---
 include/ui/console.h |  1 +
 ui/console.c         | 14 ++++++++++++++
 ui/dbus.c            |  1 +
 3 files changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/ui/console.h b/include/ui/console.h
index 363495694..4156a3b54 100644
--- a/include/ui/console.h
+++ b/include/ui/console.h
@@ -369,6 +369,7 @@ QemuConsole *qemu_console_lookup_by_device_name(const char *device_id,
                                                 uint32_t head, Error **errp);
 QEMUCursor *qemu_console_get_cursor(QemuConsole *con);
 bool qemu_console_is_graphic(QemuConsole *con);
+bool qemu_console_requires_gl(QemuConsole *con);
 bool qemu_console_is_fixedsize(QemuConsole *con);
 bool qemu_console_is_gl_blocked(QemuConsole *con);
 char *qemu_console_get_label(QemuConsole *con);
diff --git a/ui/console.c b/ui/console.c
index a8a2a247d..14e753213 100644
--- a/ui/console.c
+++ b/ui/console.c
@@ -1284,6 +1284,20 @@ bool qemu_console_is_graphic(QemuConsole *con)
     return con && QEMU_IS_GRAPHIC_CONSOLE(con);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Whether the device behind this console needs a GL context to be
+ * displayed at all, as opposed to merely being able to use one. Only a
+ * virtio-gpu with virgl enabled sets GRAPHIC_FLAGS_GL; a plain VGA or
+ * virtio-vga does not.
+ */
+bool qemu_console_requires_gl(QemuConsole *con)
+{
+    if (!con || !con->hw_ops || !con->hw_ops->get_flags) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    return con->hw_ops->get_flags(con->hw) & GRAPHIC_FLAGS_GL;
+}
+
 bool qemu_console_is_fixedsize(QemuConsole *con)
 {
     return con && (QEMU_IS_GRAPHIC_CONSOLE(con) || QEMU_IS_FIXED_TEXT_CONSOLE(con));
diff --git a/ui/dbus.c b/ui/dbus.c
index 7be0f8e26..721426027 100644
--- a/ui/dbus.c
+++ b/ui/dbus.c
@@ -198,6 +198,7 @@ dbus_display_add_console(DBusDisplay *dd, QemuConsole *con, Error **errp)
     }
 
     if (qemu_console_is_graphic(con) &&
+        qemu_console_requires_gl(con) &&
         dd->gl_mode != DISPLAY_GL_MODE_OFF) {
         qemu_console_set_display_gl_ctx(con, &dd->glctx);
     }
